Did you watch the tape?

262
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:55,850
No.

263
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:02,780
The selection committee has chosen the three of you as our finalists.

264
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:06,610
The decision will be based on the answers you give to the questions I ask.

265
00:13:06,780 --> 00:13:10,910
We'll start with Dr. Li. You claim the field is too reliant...

266
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:14,950
...on the Linnaean taxonomic system. How do you propose to correct this?

267
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:18,290
I believe that the answers lie in the osteological evidence.

268
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:20,290
I plan to begin there.

269
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:20,290
Interesting.

270
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:22,750
I guess.

271
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:27,300
Dr. Biely, your proposal includes some fieldwork. Where might that take place?

272
00:13:27,470 --> 00:13:30,180
Primarily in the Pierre Shale region of South Dakota.

273
00:13:30,350 --> 00:13:34,810
Certainly. Very well. And Dr. Geller, when is my birthday?

274
00:13:41,230 --> 00:13:43,020
What? I... Uh.

275
00:13:45,030 --> 00:13:47,200
Care to venture a guess?

276
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:53,740
May 12?

277
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:53,740
That's not even kind of close.

278
00:13:54,790 --> 00:13:57,120
Dr. Li, how many graduate students will you need?

279
00:13:57,330 --> 00:13:59,290
Half a dozen.

280
00:13:57,330 --> 00:13:59,290
I see. And Dr. Biely?

281
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:01,790
Three for excavation, and two for analysis.

282
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:05,800
Certainly. Dr. Geller, which 1965 Shirelles hit...

283
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:09,180
...was later covered by a popular British Invasion band?

284
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:12,800
What?

285
00:14:12,970 --> 00:14:15,470
What? I need six graduate students.

286
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:19,390
No, I'm sorry. We were looking for "Baby It's You."

287
00:14:19,810 --> 00:14:20,980
"Baby It's You."

288
00:14:22,770 --> 00:14:24,900
What? Wait just a minute.

289
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:28,280
None of my questions have anything to do with paleontology.

290
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:30,950
You're right, I apologize. Scratch the last question.

291
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:33,320
Spell "Boscodictiasaur."

292
00:14:34,580 --> 00:14:38,910
Um, I've never heard of a "Boscodictiasaur."

293
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:41,120
Yeah, I just made it up. Spell it.

294
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:47,760
Okay. B-O...

295
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:47,760
No, it starts with a silent M.

296
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:50,090
Oh, come on!

297
00:14:56,810 --> 00:15:00,480
I can't believe Joey. I hate being called a liar.

298
00:15:00,690 --> 00:15:02,060
But you are a liar.

299
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:05,360
What did I just say?

300
00:15:06,610 --> 00:15:08,070
Are you still here?

301
00:15:06,610 --> 00:15:08,070
Yes.

302
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:12,700
And I'm not just hurt, I'm insulted. When I tell somebody I did something...

303
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:17,040
Okay, hold on, let me just stop you right there, okay? First, you lied. Right?

304
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:19,790
Then you lied about lying, okay?

305
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:22,870
Then you lied about lying about lying, okay?

306
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:28,590
So before you lie about lying about lying about lying about lying...

307
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:32,340
Stop lying.

308
00:15:32,510 --> 00:15:35,140
Why are you so sure I didn't watch this tape?

309
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:37,510
You wanna know why? You wanna know why?

310
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:39,850
Well, this is going well.

311
00:15:41,310 --> 00:15:42,980
Here's how I know.

312
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:48,020
If you had seen what was on this tape, believe me, you'd have some comments.

313
00:15:48,190 --> 00:15:50,990
All right, remember, I got paid a lot of money for this...

314
00:15:51,150 --> 00:15:53,570
...and it only aired in Japan.

315
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,240
Ichiban.

316
00:15:57,280 --> 00:16:15,260
Ichiban, lipstick for men.

317
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:21,390
And that's how I know you didn't watch the tape.

318
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:26,850
He really is a chameleon.

319
00:16:33,780 --> 00:16:37,990
Well, Gladys, say hello to your new home.

320
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:43,910
Oh, my.

321
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:43,910
Wow.

322
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:47,880
Oh, she is so nice and big.

323
00:16:49,090 --> 00:16:55,260
Oh, Monica, where are you going to display Gladys, oh, so proudly?

324
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:58,720
I haven't really settled on a spot yet.

325
00:16:58,930 --> 00:17:00,560
How about right above the TV?

326
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:05,230
That way, it will be the first thing that you see when you walk in the door.

327
00:17:06,350 --> 00:17:09,940
Yeah, yeah, and you can get rid of that French poster.

328
00:17:10,110 --> 00:17:12,030
I like that poster.

329
00:17:10,110 --> 00:17:12,030
Really?

330
00:17:12,530 --> 00:17:14,610
It doesn't have anything coming out of it.

331
00:17:15,490 --> 00:17:18,160
Or maybe there's someplace for her in your bedroom?

332
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:21,030
Oh, there's nothing above your bed.

333
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:21,030
Are you still here?

334
00:17:25,710 --> 00:17:27,500
Oh, hi. Hello.

335
00:17:27,670 --> 00:17:31,420
Uh, have you come to ask me some more paleontology-related questions?

336
00:17:31,590 --> 00:17:34,210
Um, your grandmother's nickname, perhaps?

337
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:36,130
Ann-Margret's pant size?

338
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:43,010
I've come here to apologize. I think I may have let my feelings...

339
00:17:43,180 --> 00:17:46,060
...for Charlie interfere with the interview process.

340
00:17:46,230 --> 00:17:48,350
No. Stop!

341
00:17:49,060 --> 00:17:51,980
Anyway, I decided to offer you the grant.

342
00:17:53,690 --> 00:17:58,150
Really?

343
00:17:53,690 --> 00:17:58,150
There is just, uh, one small stipulation.

344
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:01,450
I have to break up with Charlie?

345
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:01,450
Hey, you got one right.

346
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:08,410
You're crazy.

347
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:08,410
Crazy or romantic?

348
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:10,250
Crazy.

349
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:14,460
Or?

350
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:14,460
Get out!

351
00:18:21,390 --> 00:18:22,470
Oh, my God!

352
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:28,940
What?

353
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:28,940
Joey, what is this thing doing here?

354
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:33,940
I got her from Monica. She sold it to me for a very reasonable price.

355
00:18:34,110 --> 00:18:37,740
Joey, we're not keeping this.

356
00:18:34,110 --> 00:18:37,740
But it's an original Buffay.

357
00:18:40,950 --> 00:18:43,660
All right, fine. You can keep it.

358
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:46,200
As long as you don't mind that she's haunted.

359
00:18:46,370 --> 00:18:47,870
Hey, what? Whoa. What?

360
00:18:48,410 --> 00:18:52,830
Well, legend has it, Joey, that she comes alive when you're asleep.

361
00:18:55,210 --> 00:18:58,130
She climbs out of the frame...

362
00:18:58,300 --> 00:19:02,550
...and then drags her half-a-body across the floor...

363
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:04,550
...just looking for legs to steal.

364
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:08,350
And then with her one good hand...

365
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:12,520
...she slowly reaches up...

366
00:19:12,690 --> 00:19:14,940
...and turns your doorknob.

367
00:19:15,110 --> 00:19:18,730
Get that legless witch out of here!

368
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:27,330
Hey, I sold that to Joey.

369
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:27,330
Yeah, well, I told him it's haunted.

370
00:19:27,490 --> 00:19:30,500
Two can play at this game.

371
00:19:27,490 --> 00:19:30,500
Too late. You can't give it back.

372
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:32,920
Oh, yes, I can.

373
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:32,920
No, you can't, she's yours.

374
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:34,330
She's yours.

375
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:34,330
She's yours.

376
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:37,000
She's yours.

377
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:37,000
Hey.

378
00:19:38,550 --> 00:19:42,130
She's mine.

379
00:19:38,550 --> 00:19:42,130
She's mine.

380
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:45,430
You guys, you don't have to fight over her anymore.

381
00:19:45,930 --> 00:19:49,310
Whoever doesn't get Gladys, gets Glynnis.

382
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:58,980
I want Gladys.

383
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:58,980
She's mine.

384
00:19:59,150 --> 00:20:00,320
She's mine.

385
00:19:59,150 --> 00:20:00,320
She's mine.

386
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:07,950
Look, I'm sorry I didn't give them your tape.

387
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:12,160
And I promise next time to submit you, whether I think you're right or not.

388
00:20:12,330 --> 00:20:15,290
That's not the point, Chandler. The point is that you lied.

389
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:17,290
I know. You're right.

390
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:20,050
Oh, what's it gonna take for you to forgive me?

391
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:21,340
Oh, my God.

392
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:27,640
Oh, excellent.

393
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:31,020
Now what do you say?

394
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:33,390
Lying is wrong.

395
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:36,020
And? And?

396
00:20:37,810 --> 00:20:39,570
I'm a pretty little girl.

397
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:43,690
I knew it. Ha, ha.

398
00:20:51,330 --> 00:20:53,750
Your ex-boyfriend is insane.

399
00:20:55,330 --> 00:20:57,790
Did you get the grant?

400
00:20:55,330 --> 00:20:57,790
No. And you wanna know why?

401
00:20:57,960 --> 00:21:01,340
Because your ex-boyfriend is still in love with you.

402
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:02,550
What?

403
00:21:02,710 --> 00:21:05,090
He refused me because I wouldn't give you up.

404
00:21:05,260 --> 00:21:08,470
Benji isn't in love with me. I mean, he broke up with me.

405
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:12,890
And besides, he's a very ethical man.

406
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:12,890
Really?

407
00:21:13,810 --> 00:21:16,480
Is it ethical to ask someone in a grant review:

408
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:18,520
"Who was the voice of Underdog?"

409
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:20,860
I'm sure he was just joking.

410
00:21:21,020 --> 00:21:23,360
If you don't believe me, let's go talk to him.

411
00:21:23,530 --> 00:21:26,570
I'm telling you, he didn't ask me one paleontological question.

412
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:29,820
Seriously?

413
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:29,820
Oh, I'm sorry. No, he did ask me one:

414
00:21:29,990 --> 00:21:32,160
Uh, "How do you spell Boscodictiasaur?"

415
00:21:32,330 --> 00:21:35,870
Well, if it's like the Lake Mbosco in Congo, then M-B-O...

416
00:21:36,040 --> 00:21:37,210
Damn it.

417
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:44,090
Dr. Geller. Charlie, what are you doing here?

418
00:21:44,260 --> 00:21:46,130
I want you to tell her everything.

419
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:50,010
About the deal you tried to make with me, about the crazy questions you...

420
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:55,470
Wally Cox. That's the voice of Underdog.

421
00:21:56,270 --> 00:21:58,350
Like I tried to tell you in the interview...

422
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:02,610
...this grant is not based on your knowledge of pretty useless trivia.

423
00:22:02,770 --> 00:22:07,650
No, don't do that. I want you to look her in the eyes and tell her the truth.

424
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:09,950
Benji?

425
00:22:11,160 --> 00:22:15,910
It's true. I behaved horribly, but it's only because I still love you.

426
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:19,080
And I would do anything to have you back in my life.

427
00:22:19,250 --> 00:22:21,880
Too little, too late, Benji.

428
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:27,130
I can't believe this.

429
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:27,130
I never should've broken up with you.

430
00:22:27,300 --> 00:22:32,350
I think about you all the time. Do you ever still think about me?

431
00:22:32,510 --> 00:22:34,140
No.

432
00:22:34,930 --> 00:22:37,180
Yes.

433
00:22:34,930 --> 00:22:37,180
What?

434
00:22:38,020 --> 00:22:41,900
I don't know what to say, Benji. This is all so...

435
00:22:42,060 --> 00:22:44,270
...romantic.

436
00:22:44,730 --> 00:22:46,820
Or?

437
00:22:48,990 --> 00:22:51,200
I know I may be way out of bounds here...

438
00:22:51,370 --> 00:22:54,830
...but is there any chance you would take me back?

439
00:22:57,450 --> 00:22:59,290
Maybe.

440
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:03,580
Sweetie, this conversation is starting to make me a little uncomfortable.

441
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:09,050
Oh, God. I am so sorry, but...

442
00:23:09,220 --> 00:23:14,010
I mean, there's so much history between us, you know?

443
00:23:14,180 --> 00:23:16,600
I'm sorry too.

444
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:28,320
I love you.

445
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:28,320
Oh, I love you too.

446
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:33,410
Okay, that's it, we are seeing other people.

447
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:54,760
Gladys?

448
00:24:01,810 --> 00:24:05,560
For the third time this week. Man, this does not get old.

449
00:24:06,940 --> 00:24:10,900
You're mean!

450
00:24:06,940 --> 00:24:10,900
Oh, don't be such a baby. Please.

